{"id": "api-ionos-key-is-prefix-dot-secret", "type": "api_behavior", "fact": "The IONOS API key is a single string of the form '<prefix>.<secret>'. certbot-dns-ionos wants the two halves split across dns_ionos_prefix and dns_ionos_secret, plus dns_ionos_endpoint (https://api.hosting.ionos.com, same for every account). The failure mode discriminates the cause: MISSING properties means the ini was written with the wrong key names (the pre-2.3.2 dns_ionos_api_key/api_secret form, see gotcha-certbot-latest-flag-drift); 401/403 means the halves are swapped or the whole key was pasted into one field.", "recommendation": "Store the public prefix in 'pass ionos/api-key' (or IONOS_API_KEY) and the secret in 'pass ionos/api-secret' (or IONOS_API_SECRET) - the names are misleading, api-key holds the PREFIX. Validate credentials without spending a Let's Encrypt rate limit: curl -s -H \"X-API-Key: <prefix>.<secret>\" https://api.hosting.ionos.com/dns/v1/zones - JSON zone list means good, 401 means swapped, 403 means the contract has no DNS API access enabled.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "production session production: first working IONOS DNS-01 integration + auto-renewal", "date": "2026-09-09"}], "tags": ["ionos", "certbot", "dns-01", "credentials", "letsencrypt"], "affectedFiles": ["commands/proxy.sh", "easyhome/ionos-config-helper.sh"], "affectedServices": [], "createdAt": "2026-09-09T00:00:00Z", "updatedAt": "2026-09-09T00:00:00Z", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
